e0$ be one of those coefficients. By [F3] the number of primitive elements of $\mathbb F_{p^d}^	imes$ is $\varphi(p^d-1)$, which is unbounded and satisfies $\varphi(N)\ge\sqrt{N/2}$ (factor $N$ over prime powers: each factor $\varphi(r^a)^2/r^a=r^{a-2}(r-1)^2\ge1$ except $r=2$, $a=1$, where it is $1/2$). Choose $d$ with $\varphi(p^d-1)>\deg g$ and $p^d-1$ larger than every $U$-degree of $f$; then some primitive $z\in\mathbb F_{p^d}^	imes$ avoids the roots of $g$. Repeated one-variable root bounds on the nonzero-coordinate grid (each $U_a$ is constrained to be a power $z^{c_a}
