Triangular symmetric lifts. Index colored cycle types by partitions $\mu$ obtained by replacing each cycle of length $a$ and color $r$ by $k=(a-1)\ell+r$ and discarding zero parts. These are exactly the partitions satisfying $N(\mu)=\operatorname{length}(\mu)+\sum_j\lfloor\mu_j/\ellfloor\le d$; the inverse adds $d-N(\mu)$ trivial fixed points. Put $D(\mu)=\sum_j(\mu_j-\lfloor\mu_j/\ellfloor)$ and $p_\mu=\sum_{
u\sim(\mu,0,\dots,0)}x_1^{
u_1}\cdots x_d^{
u_d}$, summing each distinct exponent tuple once. It is central by step 1.2 and lies in filtration degree $D(\mu)$ by step 4.1. Its symbol at that degree is $z_\mu$ plus orbit sums with strictly smaller $N$: each product of the leading star cycles on disjoint supports has the prescribed type, and its coefficient is one, since each cycle's largest vertex uniquely chooses its star hub, its ordered other vertices uniquely choose its star expansion, and the unordered exponent tuple chooses each assignment only once, even for repeated parts. Overlapping supports strictly decrease the number of used vertices, as does every error from step 4.1; disjoint-cycle reduction preserves this bound. The entire symbol is central, so the remainder is a combination of orbit sums by step 3.1, with smaller $N$ and the same homogeneous degree. Hence, ordering the finite colored types by $N$, the symbols of the $p_\mu$ form a unit triangular change of the orbit-sum basis, degree by degree. [step 1.2, step 3.1, step 4.1, algebra]

